[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:But not Murder!]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:11.05]Do you think that the writer passed his driving test? Why? | 你认为作者通过了驾驶考试吗？为什么？
[00:18.03]I was being tested for a driving licence for the third time. | 我正在参加第三次驾驶执照考试。
[00:23.38]I had been asked to drive in heavy traffic and had done so successfully. | 我被要求在交通繁忙的地方驾车，我成功地做到了。
[00:30.18]After having been instructed to drive out of town, I began to acquire confidence. | 在接到出城的指令后，我开始有了信心。
[00:37.95]Sure that I had passed, I was almost beginning to enjoy my test. | 确信自己已通过考试，我几乎开始喜欢这次考试了。
[00:45.04]The examiner must have been pleased with my performance, for he smiled and said, 'Just one more thing Mr. Eames. | 主考人显然对我的表现很满意，因为他微笑着说：“埃姆斯先生，还剩最后一项。
[00:55.66]Let us suppose that a child suddenly crosses the road in front of you. | 我们假设一个小孩突然穿过你前面的马路。
[01:01.75]As soon as I tap on the window, you must stop within five feet.' | 我一敲车窗，你就必须在5英尺之内把车停下来。”
[01:08.32]I continued driving and after some time, the examiner tapped loudly. | 我继续开着车，过了一会儿，主考人使劲敲起车窗来。
[01:14.64]Though the sound could be heard clearly, it took me a long time to react. | 虽然声音听得很清楚，但我过了好一会儿才作出反应。
[01:21.62]I suddenly pressed the brake pedal hard and we were both thrown forward. | 我猛地踩下刹车踏板，我们两人都向前冲去。
[01:27.64]The examiner looked at me sadly. | 主考人伤心地看着我。
[01:31.22]'Mr. Eames,' he said, in a mournful voice, 'you have just killed that child!' | “埃姆斯先生，”他以悲痛的声调说，“你刚刚把那个小孩压死了！”
